their lead coming up to the 875-metres mark, but the race ended in an easy victory for the Hungarians, led by their anchor swimmer, " [:a {:href "/athletes/48187"} "Zoltán Halmay"] ". They were almost 24 seconds ahead of the second placed German team, with Great Britain third."] "\n\n" [:p {} "For many years, it was not known what format the relay took, but the discovery of an article in the Austrian newspaper " [:em {} "Allgemeine Sport-Zeitung"] " from 1906 revealed that not only did the race take place in an “unruly” sea with high waves in the open bay, but the swimmers swam out to a 125 m turning point before returning to the start. After each swimmer had completed 250 m, he handed over to the next member of their team."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "Hungary"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HUN.png"}] "HUN"]] [:td {} "16:52.4"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:class "bib"} "844"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/48227"} "József Ónody"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "–"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:class "bib"} "808"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/48185"} "Henrik Hajós"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "–"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:class "bib"} "819"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/48202"} "Géza Kiss"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "–"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:class "bib"} "807"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/48187"} "Zoltán Halmay"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "–"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {: